From 34bb1ded7e1304a92301dbb2c9933f7bb81c6f39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gaius Mulley <gaiusmod2@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:48:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PR modula2/128293: Document plugin/m2rte.so dynamically
 linked to stdc++

This patch for doc/install.texi documents that m2rte.so is
dependent upon stdc++.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	PR modula2/128293
	* doc/install.texi (GM2-prerequisite): Add paragraph
	explaining m2rte.so is dependent upon stdc++.

(cherry picked from commit a6c50b0dde127f7e1c60d480de5fc4b4629aa6f2)

Signed-off-by: Gaius Mulley <gaiusmod2@gmail.com>
---
 gcc/doc/install.texi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gcc/doc/install.texi b/gcc/doc/install.texi
index 41424773b0a8..46d466e657cc 100644
--- a/gcc/doc/install.texi
+++ b/gcc/doc/install.texi
@@ -346,6 +346,12 @@ documentation including the target @code{SYSTEM} definition module.
 If Python3 is unavailable Modula-2 documentation will include a target
 independent version of the SYSTEM modules.
 
+If plugins are enabled a compile time call flow analysis shared
+library @file{m2rte.so} is built.  This plugin performs a limited
+amount of compile time static analysis in an attempt to detect runtime
+Modula-2 exceptions at compile time.  The plugin @file{m2rte.so}
+depends upon @file{-lstdc++}.
+
 @item @anchor{gccrs-prerequisite}gccrs
 
 The official Rust compiler and Rust build system (cargo) are required for
